# The frame flow's one-minute cadence (storage-map §4d `sync-frame-videos`:
# "The panel checks EVERY MINUTE: share reachable? new content? -> fetch/mirror;
# unreachable (box asleep) = skip silently, never wake").
#
# THE FIRST TIMER THIS PANEL HAS EVER SHIPPED, and that is a deliberate exception
# rather than a reversal: OI-15's "there is deliberately NO periodic timer" is
# about the MUSIC pull it was written for, whose source is always-on and whose
# first sync is the whole library. It does not describe the frame flow, which the
# storage map had already put on a one-minute clock before OI-18 made two mounts
# possible at all.
#
# OnUnitInactiveSec, not OnCalendar and NOT OnUnitActiveSec: the period is "a
# minute after the last run FINISHED". OnUnitActiveSec was wrong for that claim
# and the comment here used to assert it anyway — it measures from ACTIVATION, so
# a run that takes longer than a minute re-fires the moment it exits, and a run
# that consistently takes 90 s would have this timer permanently at zero delay.
# OnUnitInactiveSec measures from DEACTIVATION, which is what the storage map's
# "check every minute" means for a job whose duration is not fixed. (The per-flow
# lock in wall-sync.sh is the belt to this braces — systemd will not run two
# instances of one unit, but wall-sync.service mirrors the frame flow too.)
#
# Persistent= is deliberately ABSENT. It would fire a catch-up run at boot for
# every minute the panel spent suspended overnight — systemd coalesces that into
# ONE run, so it is not a storm, but it is also pointless: wall-sync.service
# already mirrors both flows at boot and wall-sync-resume.service does it again
# on every wake. OnBootSec below is the only start-up trigger this needs, and it
# is late enough not to race the boot sync for the lock.
[Unit]
Description=Wall panel: check the frame-video share every minute (OI-18 / storage-map 4d)
Documentation=file:///opt/wall-panel/stack/autoinstall/wall/README.md

[Timer]
OnBootSec=3min
OnUnitInactiveSec=1min
AccuracySec=10s
Unit=wall-sync-frame.service

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
